        solution: "First calculate the guideline amounts for a complete bread-and-cheese party. Thirty-six guests require 36 × 1/6 = 6 French sticks and 36 × 40 g = 1440 g of cheese. Because guests bring other food, Dina supplies one third of both totals: 6/3 = 2 sticks and 1440/3 = 480 g. This is B.\nA uses only 240 g of cheese, too little. C does not apply the stated one-third reduction correctly to either total. D gives the full guideline amounts rather than Dina's share. E gives far too much bread. Apply the same reduction to each component; the fact that the quantities use different units does not change the fraction the host provides.",
